{
    "_id": "cinder-bloom",
    "name": "Cinder Bloom",
    "instructions": "1. Place 4 ají dulce peppers in a shaker and muddle. Add the rest of the ingredients along with ice. Shake hard for about 5 seconds, or until the outside of the shaker is frosty. Strain into the glass over ice.",
    "created_at": null,
    "updated_at": null,
    "description": "\"The inspiration behind this cocktail began with my love for the Margarita,\" says Omar Bautista, beverage manager of Boro Brine in New York City. Using the tequila classic as a template, he layered the bold flavors of passion fruit and Aperol with the sweet vegetal notes of ají peppers for a refreshing and aromatic cocktail. Bautista says that any tropical pepper will work, too, or swap in red or yellow bell peppers for a more vegetal profile.",
